"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/ci.yml","summary":"Adds the canary-guards step to test-macos.","annotations":[{"newRange":[71,76],"summary":"test-macos fetches full history and runs canary-guards beside test and build.","rationale":"The canary diffs against origin/main, so a shallow clone would fail it. The pre-rebase head passed test-macos in run 38449578130. The rebased head is checked by the new CI run.","author":"fm/verilex-macos-canary-guards"}]},
{"path":"scripts/canary-guards","summary":"Fixes two macOS-only failures the new step exposed.","annotations":[{"newRange":[20,25],"summary":"plant replaces text with prefix and suffix slicing instead of quoted pattern replacement.","rationale":"macOS bash 3.2 keeps the quotes in ${code/\"$2\"/\"$3\"} as text, so planted attacks broke the scratch copy and gave false reds. scripts/canary-guards passes on Linux after the rebase.","author":"fm/verilex-macos-canary-guards"},{"newRange":[84,84],"summary":"The proc-cwd guard is skipped where /proc/self/cwd does not exist.","rationale":"That attack cannot occur without /proc, so the guard gave a false red on macOS. Linux still runs it.","author":"fm/verilex-macos-canary-guards"}]}]}
